---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import { buttonClass, demoClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';
---
<MotionPage title="Motion: SVG" description="Motions on SVG elements: drawing a stroke, travelling along a path, and morphing one path into another.">
  <h1>SVG</h1>
  <p>A motion binds on an SVG element as it does on an HTML one, with three exceptions: a layout motion is refused there, since it needs a box; a split plays the element whole, since its text is not cut; and values, sequences and gestures bind to HTML elements only. Two visual fields are for shapes and paths.</p>

  <h2>Draw</h2>
  <p><code>draw</code>, from 0 to 1, draws a path or a basic shape from nothing to its whole stroke. It sets <code>pathLength</code> to 1 and the dash of the stroke. A finished draw at 1 gives both back to the author at rest, and a binding gives them back when it is destroyed. The preset <code>draw</code> is an <code>appear</code> from nothing to the whole stroke.</p>
  <pre><code>{`<path data-motion="draw" d="M16 25L22 31L33 19"/>`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Along a path</h2>
  <p><code>along</code>, from 0 to 1, moves an element along the <code>offset-path</code> its CSS gives it, by writing <code>offset-distance</code>. An element that is on the page when the runtime connects keeps the <code>offset-distance</code> its CSS gives it: set <code>offset-distance: 100%</code> on a travel that should rest at its end.</p>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

// The element travels from the start of its offset path to its end
defineMotion('travel', { verb: 'appear', keyframes: [{ along: 0 }, { along: 1 }] });`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Morph</h2>
  <p><code>morph(path, to, &#123; timing, precision &#125;)</code>, from <code>@udixio/motion/svg</code>, morphs the <code>d</code> of a path into the <code>d</code> of another path element, or into a <code>d</code> string. Both shapes are resampled with anime.js, so they need not have the same number of points. The default timing is <code>spring.default.spatial</code>; a curve is its own easing. The path must be inside an SVG.</p>
  <pre><code>{`import { morph } from '@udixio/motion/svg';

const handle = morph(icon, 'M7 5 H10 V19 H7 Z M14 5 H17 V19 H14 Z');
await handle.finished; // 'finished' once the shape is there
handle.cancel();       // leaves the shape where it is`}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>precision</code> is the number of points per unit of length the shapes are sampled at; 0 morphs the two strings as they are.</li>
    <li>The handle ends when the shape is there, and the path then carries exactly the <code>d</code> of the target.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>The icon morphs between a play triangle and a pause mark. Its button says which shape the icon shows, with <code>aria-pressed</code>.</p>
  <div class={demoClass}>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-16 text-primary" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path data-svg-morph d="M8 5 L19 12 L8 19 Z" />
      </svg>
      <button type="button" class={buttonClass} data-svg-morph-button aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Morph the icon between play and pause">Morph</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>The live draw and travel examples are on the <a href="/motion/demo#demo-svg">demo</a>.</p>

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>Under reduced motion an entry or an exit with <code>draw</code> sets its stroke at once and fades only the opacity, and an <code>along</code> moves at once and fades in place. <code>morph</code> sets the shape at once under reduced motion, with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, or with a zero motion scale.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A layout motion is refused on an SVG element.</li>
    <li>Two motions that draw one shape share its <code>pathLength</code>: it stays 1 while either draws.</li>
    <li><code>morph</code> needs anime.js, which the consumer installs alongside the package.</li>
  </ul>

  <script>
    import { morph } from '@udixio/motion/svg';

    // The two icons the morph joins: a play triangle and a pause mark, in the same 24 by 24 box.
    const PLAY = 'M8 5 L19 12 L8 19 Z';
    const PAUSE = 'M7 5 H10 V19 H7 Z M14 5 H17 V19 H14 Z';
    // The morph in progress, if any: a new morph replaces it from the shape it has reached.
    let morphing: ReturnType<typeof morph> | undefined;

    document.addEventListener('click', event => {
      if (!(event.target instanceof Element)) return;
      const button = event.target.closest<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-svg-morph-button]');
      if (!button) return;
      const pressed = button.getAttribute('aria-pressed') !== 'true';
      button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(pressed));
      const icon = document.querySelector<SVGPathElement>('[data-svg-morph]');
      if (!icon) return;
      morphing?.cancel();
      morphing = morph(icon, pressed ? PAUSE : PLAY);
    });
  </script>
</MotionPage>
